  "caption": "Uncle Quinn got a text: nephew Pip has a small curve in his spine. Cue panic-googling, and guilt about heavy bags and slouching.\n\nKay's calmer take: most teen curves are small and mainly need monitoring, and bags, posture or sport don't cause them. The key time to watch is while kids are still growing.\n\nWhat can help: keep playing sport, stick to the check-up schedule from the GP or specialist, focus on comfort and consistent wear if a brace is prescribed, and keep expectations realistic. A lighter bag may help comfort but won't change the curve.\n\nGet it checked if the curve looks clearly worse, or there's significant or night pain, leg weakness or numbness, or bladder or bowel changes.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
